HEURISTIC product model: N_ij(K) ~ c_ij * N_i.(K) N_.j(K) / K with Landau marginals
  N_i.(K) ~ (3K/log 6K) L^{i-1}/(i-1)!  =>  N_ij ~ c * (9K/log^2 6K) L^{i+j-2}/((i-1)!(j-1)!)
  Landau weights w_ij = L^{i+j-2}/((i-1)!(j-1)!) for the nine cells:
   (1,1):1  (1,2)=(2,1):L  (2,2):L^2  (1,3)=(3,1):L^2/2  (2,3)=(3,2):L^3/2  (3,3):L^4/4
  Pairs (i,j),(j,i) tie exactly (symmetric weight).  (2,2) vs (1,3): factor 1 vs 1/2.
  Threshold crossings under Landau weights: (3,3)=(2,3)=(2,2) all at L=2 (K=e^{e^2}/6=269.7~270);
  (2,2)>(1,2) for L>1; (3,3)>(1,1) for L>sqrt(2); CC>PS for L^3>4 i.e. L>1.587.
  Landau predicted nine-cell order for L>2:  CC > CS=SC > SS > CP=PC > PS=SP > PP
  Landau predicted MERGED six-class order: SC+CS > CC > SS = PC+CP > PS+SP > PP for 2<L<4
    (CC = L^4/4 vs SC+CS = L^3: CC first in the merged order only for L>4, x=exp(exp(4))~10^23.7)
  Landau predicted order for 1<L<2: SS > CS=SC > CC ...  (see actual data below)
  STATUS: HEURISTIC (Hardy-Littlewood-type product with a common singular series);
          the marginal Landau term itself is very inaccurate at these scales (table above).

