When does the SD-F6 product model (c=1) reach the Landau asymptotic order CC > SC+CS > SS > ...?
  CC > SS  (w3 > w2)         at L = 3.1699, i.e. x = 6K = exp(exp(L)) ~ 10^10.3
  CC > SC+CS (w3 > 2 w2)     at L = 4.9285, i.e. x = 6K = exp(exp(L)) ~ 10^60.0
  SS > PS+SP (w2 > 2 w1)     at L = 2.5718, i.e. x = 6K = exp(exp(L)) ~ 10^5.7
  (actual SS > PS+SP for good after K=920807, x~10^6.74; the c=1 model puts it at x~10^5.68: about one decade early.)
  STATUS: HEURISTIC; the CC-on-top order of the naive heuristic is a ~10^60 phenomenon under SD-F6.

==============================================================================
4. Tournament audit (repo guardrail)
==============================================================================
Score sequences of all 64 labelled tournaments on 4 vertices: [(0, 1, 2, 3), (0, 2, 2, 2), (1, 1, 1, 3), (1, 1, 2, 2)]
One-line proof: scores sum to C(4,2)=6, so profile (b,m,m,a) with 0<=a<m<b<=3 needs a+2m+b=6;
  integer solutions with a<m<b in {0,1,2,3}: [] (none).  Enumeration above is the check.
PROVED/FINITE-EXACT: no 4-vertex tournament has score profile (max, mid, mid, min) with
  max > mid > min.  The user's 'max, min, two equal middles' is therefore not the score
  profile of any tournament; it is a weak order (total preorder) with one tie, i.e. a
  transitive comparability digraph on 4 vertices with 5 arcs, not 6.
Intrinsic relations between cells: the involution iota: k -> -k maps cell (i,j) to (j,i)
  (inherited SW2; |6(-k)-1| = 6k+1).  On the nine cells iota has 3 fixed points (PP,SS,CC) and 3
  2-cycles; it is symmetric, so it orients nothing, and it leaves the positive prefix 1<=k<=K
  (it relates the positive and the signed census, not members of two cells).  An orientation
  such as (i,j)->(j,i) for i<j is a gauge (left endpoint < right endpoint), not data.
  SCOPE: no other intrinsic pairwise relation between cells was found (a non-discovery, not a
  theorem); the non-tournament verdict itself is inherited from section SW1 of the divisors note.
Frequency ordering = a scale-dependent total preorder on the cells; at K=10000000:
  SS > CS > SC > CC > PS > SP > PC > CP > PP
VERDICT: the '4-tournament' reading is a cosmetic ranking.  It carries no content beyond the
  four counts, has no intrinsic pairwise observable, and its claimed tie is not a tournament
  feature but a heuristic asymptotic symmetry (mirror cells) that exact counts violate at
  every finite K where N_12 != N_21.

