How C changes the picture (HEURISTIC asymptotic symmetry, FINITE-EXACT order):
  asymptotic ties by mirror symmetry: PS~SP, PC~CP, SC~CS (3 tied pairs); PP,SS,CC unpaired.
  Ranks at K=10^3..10^7 (1 = most frequent):
    nine SS: [1, 1, 1, 1, 1]
    nine CC: [9, 9, 8, 6, 4]
    six SS:  [2, 2, 3, 2, 2]
    six CC:  [6, 6, 5, 5, 5]
  Landau's nine-cell leading order for L>2 puts CC on top.  Actual: in the nine-cell ranking SS is
  first at every decade and CC rises from ninth (10^3, 10^4) to eighth, sixth, fourth (10^7); in the
  merged six-class ranking SS is second (third at 10^5) and CC sixth (10^3, 10^4) then fifth
  (10^5..10^7).  Only at 10^7 does the nine-cell order read SS > CS > SC > CC > ... (CC overtakes
  PC/CP and PP early; see crossover table).
  With C the 2x2 'max, min, two middles' becomes a 9-cell preorder with three symmetric pairs
  and three singletons: 6 classes, of which only the pairs are asymptotically tied.

